Additionally, the Desktop Recording SDK also handles a long tail of edge cases, including network interruptions. By uploading meeting data while the recording is happening, the SDK saves the portion of the recording captured before a network interruption, rather than losing the entire recording. The capabilities covered in this blog address reliability issues developers face when building and maintaining a desktop meeting recorder.


